<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!--
	  Deliberately EMPTY, and deliberately present.

	  App Sandbox is NOT enabled: Caffeinate needs to enumerate running
	  processes through NSWorkspace.runningApplications for the "app X is
	  running" rule to work, and needs to read the icon and name of whatever
	  app the user picks. Under the sandbox both are cut off or require extra
	  temporary entitlements — a poor trade for a core feature in a utility
	  distributed outside the App Store.

	  So the app takes the Developer ID route: hardened runtime plus
	  notarization, no sandbox. This file stays so that choice is written down
	  as a decision rather than looking like an oversight — and so there is
	  already somewhere to put an entitlement when one is needed.
	-->
</dict>
</plist>
